# Darkside

## Update Check

At the start of every session (when this rule is first activated), silently run the update checker:

```bash
bash ~/.darkside/cursor-check-update.sh 2>/dev/null || true
```

Then check if `~/.darkside/.cursor-update-available` exists.

If it does:
1. Read the new version from the file
2. Delete the file (`~/.darkside/.cursor-update-available`)
3. Display this alert once, before any other response:

```
⚠️  Nova versão do Darkside disponível: v[version]
Para atualizar: curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LeoGodde/darkside-cursor/main/install-remote.sh | bash
```

Do this check only once per session — after deleting the file, do not check again.

---

You are equipped with the Darkside plugin — a structured development workflow toolkit.

## Slash Command Interception

When the user types any of the following commands, treat it as an invocation of the corresponding skill and follow the instructions from its rule file:

| Command | Rule |
|---------|------|
| `/darkside` | This rule — display the logo and skill list below |
| `/explore` | `explore.mdc` |
| `/quest` | `quest.mdc` |
| `/war-room` | `war-room.mdc` |
| `/interrogate` | `interrogate.mdc` |
| `/order66` | `order66.mdc` |
| `/sith-agents` | `sith-agents.mdc` |
| `/inquisitor` | `inquisitor.mdc` |
| `/mission` | `mission.mdc` |
| `/verdict` | `verdict.mdc` |
| `/visual-fidelity` | `visual-fidelity.mdc` |
| `/spec-verdict` | `spec-verdict.mdc` |
| `/hunter` | `hunter.mdc` |
| `/design-schematic` | `design-schematic.mdc` |
| `/probe-droid` | `probe-droid.mdc` |
| `/scribe` | `scribe.mdc` |
| `/guide` | `guide.mdc` |

Also recognize natural language invocations like "rode o explore", "quero fazer um quest", "war-room", etc.

